myopenmath.solution:
5040
120
\displaystyle\frac{{120}}{{5040}} (or reduced fraction \displaystyle\frac{{1}}{{42}}) or decimal 0.0238
Contestants A, B, C, D, E, F,  and G are in a 10K race.
(a) How many different ways can a race with 7 runners be completed? (Assume there is no tie.)

The order in which the runners complete the race matters so use Permutations


Number of different ways \displaystyle{7} runners can complete race =  \displaystyle{7}{P}{7}={5040} 
(b) In how many ways can D finish first and E finish second?


Ways D finishes first x Ways E finishes second x Ways that the remaining \displaystyle{5} contestants can complete the race


= 1 x 1 x \displaystyle{5}{P}{5}={120}
(c) Probability that D finishes first and E finishes second


\displaystyle=\frac{\text{Number of ways D finishes first and E finishes second}}{\text{Number of different ways 7 runners can complete race}}


\displaystyle=\frac{{120}}{{5040}}
